  "command": "OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 PYTHONPATH=../TensorDG:../TensorFEM/src:../TensorDEM/src:../TensorFVM/src:../TensorSPH/src python examples/harmonic_loaded_contact_stack.py",
  "reference": "Two 0.5 m layers of unit cross section with (k,C)=(1,1) and (4,2), separated by areal resistance 0.32. Add a spatially uniform temperature phasor to a homogeneous transfer solution and prescribe the corresponding layer generation, film ambients and wall storage. Compare four temperature traces, contact flux positive to the right and both inward wall fluxes. Check each end-wall energy balance and the contact drop. FVM additionally checks every cell mean against the exact spatial average and every cell energy balance including generation and storage. Compare the two one-sided contact fluxes. All runs use unit cross-sectional area. SPH compares particle temperatures with exact center values obtained from the analytic cell mean of the homogeneous mode. Check every slice energy balance from native rightward section fluxes and recover both interface temperatures independently by half-cell Fourier extrapolation.",
  "sph_regression": {
    "command": "OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 PYTHONPATH=src:. python -m pytest -q tests/test_conduction_2d.py",
